[center][size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]A save game manager for Cyberpunk 2077, in VS Code.[/color][/b][/size][/center]

[center]Find any save by its quest, place, lifepath, V or date. Keep sets of saves outside the game and swap them in. Give saves titles of your own.[/center]
[center][/center]
[center][size=3]One of the VS Code tools from the Edgemodders community. They all work together, with optional AI assistants.[/size][/center]
[center][/center]
[center][color=#f6b26b][size=3][i]This is an early preview release.[/i][/size][/color][/center]
[line]

[quote][size=4][b][color=#fcee0a]STATUS: NOT RELEASED YET[/color][/b][/size]
(STATUS: what has passed its hand tests, and what is new in this release.)
[b]This is not a game mod.[/b] It is an extension for VS Code, so install it there (steps below), not with Vortex. The quickest way is straight from the [url=https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=Edgemodders.redsave]VS Code Marketplace[/url] or [url=https://open-vsx.org/extension/edgemodders/redsave]Open VSX[/url]; the file here is the same extension.[/quote]

(SCREENSHOT: the save browser, with a search and filters)

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]What REDsave is[/color][/b][/size]

REDsave is built by [url=https://edgemodders.ai/]EDGEmodders[/url], a modding community whose idea is simple: [b]anyone can mod[/b]. It looks after your saves: hundreds of them, from several playthroughs, test runs for your mods and the game's own autosaves.

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Highlights[/color][/b][/size]

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]Find any save[/color][/b][/size]
Every save with its picture, its quest and place, V's lifepath, body and voice, level, Street Cred, difficulty, play time and date. Search by words, and filter by lifepath, V, playthrough, kind of save, game version, Phantom Liberty, level and date.

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]Loadouts of saves[/color][/b][/size]
Keep sets of saves outside the game's save folder: one per playthrough, one for testing a mod, one for a friend's V. Swap a set in before you play, and the one you had goes back to the library. Nothing is deleted.

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]Titles of your own[/color][/b][/size]
Call a save "Before the heist, Takemura alive" instead of a quest name, and find it again by that.

(SCREENSHOT: loadouts in the side bar)

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Install[/color][/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]In VS Code (or VSCodium, or EDGEkit), open the Extensions view (Ctrl+Shift+X).
[*]Click [b]...[/b] at its top, choose [b]Install from VSIX...[/b], and pick the .vsix from this file.
[*]Open [b]REDsave[/b] in the side bar.
[/list]

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Requirements[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Windows 10 or 11, and Cyberpunk 2077 on PC (Steam, GOG or Epic).
[*]VS Code 1.90 or later, or VSCodium, or EDGEkit.
[/list]

